Researcher fix for FV8's released patch (NOT part of FV8). Opt-in: applied by
build-node-runtime.sh only with fv8 fixes "property-case+parser-reset", after
tools/fv8/patches/V8_patch_122.diff and fv8-astnode-property-case.patch.
Apply from deps/v8 with: patch -p1 -F0 --forward

FV8 adds every declared function (FunctionLiteral*) and its name
(AstRawString*) to two process-global vectors in Parser::ParseFunctionLiteral
(parsing/parser.cc) and never clears them. Both point into the parse's Zone,
which V8 frees once that compilation finishes. AstTraversal()
(interpreter/bytecode-generator.cc) later compares names by pointer and, on a
match, reads declared_functions[i]->node_type(). Once freed Zone memory is
reused, a stale entry can match and FV8 dereferences a dangling pointer.
Observed: run 38532680501 (gdb): SIGSEGV in
BytecodeGenerator::AstTraversal <- VisitIfStatement while compiling
node:internal/options in node_mksnapshot, faulting on `mov 0x4(%rax),%eax;
and $0x3f` (reading NodeType) with rax = 0xd6000020e18df006.

This clears both vectors at the end of the Parser constructor, i.e. at the
start of every parse, so they only hold nodes of the AST that is about to be
compiled (which is alive during bytecode generation). Behaviour change: FV8
no longer follows a function name into functions declared in previously
compiled scripts or earlier parses; within one compilation (with --no-lazy,
a whole script) it still does. Not addressed: FV8's AstTraversal sorts and
de-duplicates declared_functions_names but not declared_functions, so the
index it uses can pair a name with a different function (wrong, not unsafe).

--- a/src/parsing/parser.cc
+++ b/src/parsing/parser.cc
@@ -484,6 +484,10 @@
        ++feature) {
     use_counts_[feature] = 0;
   }
+  // Researcher fix (not FV8): start each parse with empty FV8 lists, so
+  // AstTraversal only follows FunctionLiterals of the AST being compiled.
+  declared_functions.clear();
+  declared_functions_names.clear();
 }
 
 void Parser::InitializeEmptyScopeChain(ParseInfo* info) {
